# MedScale foundation

- Read `AGENTS.md` and `CURSOR.md` before material work.
- Rust is the primary and trusted-core language.
- Local-first and privacy-first are constitutional; product runtime egress is default-deny.
- Source bytes remain distinct from derived representations; source identity is not content hash.
- `Proposal != ClinicalAssertion`; AI/model/worker output has no authority by itself.
- Identity merge is explicit. Projections are rebuildable and non-authoritative.
- FHIR R4 4.0.1 is interchange, not the canonical database. External validators provide evidence only.
- One Rust authority path serves CLI/Desktop/mobile. UI/CLI/workers do not bypass it or open the canonical DB directly.
- Workers receive no ambient canonical DB, master keys, unrestricted filesystem, network, secrets, or authority.
- MESC is artifact-first and independent. Never mutate MESC from MedScale execution.
- External action `UNKNOWN` is never blindly retried.
- H0 is synthetic-only and LLM-free. Real PHI remains unauthorized until a later explicit external gate is closed.
- Never weaken an invariant to make a dependency, donor, UI framework, model, or platform easier to integrate.